     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Thanks for your help.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">I corrected it. But now I have 2\r\nquestions. </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span>1)<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">     1)\r\n</span></span></span><span dir=\"LTR\"></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">I don’t\r\nunderstand what you mean? About” </span>Also, do note the warning about the\r\nhyper parameters not being estimated (if this assumption is viable then ignore\r\nit, otherwise you should redefine the model with suitable anchors/freely\r\nestimated hyper-parameters)”<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">What is hyper\r\nparameter? Can you introduce a reference to me? I’d like to study more.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span>2)<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">     2)\r\n</span></span></span><span dir=\"LTR\"></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">My aim\r\nis to do uniform and nonuniform DIF.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">We have a*(ability-b)\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">=a</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*ability-</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">a*b</span>\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">= a</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">*ability-</span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">d ,<span>   </span>b= difficulty\r\nparameter ,d= easiness parameter.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:53.25pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span>i)<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">                   \r\n</span></span></span><span dir=\"LTR\"></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">For nonuniform\r\nDIF we test ‘a’ parameter without any concern about ‘d’.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:53.25pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><span>ii)<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">                 \r\n</span></span></span><span dir=\"LTR\"></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">But in\r\nuniform DIF we have to test ‘b’ (not d).</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:53.25pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">In fact, my question is: How can I implement uniform DIF in\r\nslope/intercept model?</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:53.25pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">How can I implement uniform DIF in mirt package?</span></p><p style=\"margin-left:53.25pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:53.25pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Please help me. I study a lot but I don’t understand it. Thanks.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:53.25pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
