   "subject": "Re: problem in DIF",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hyper parameters are parameters which describe distributions, such as the mean and variance of a Gaussian distribution. These should be estimated in order to better equate the groups. See the attached article by David Thissen describing the likelihood approach to DIF testing (using different software, but the principles are the same). </div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Phil</span><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sun, May 22, 2016 at 1:52 AM, marjan faghih <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">marjanf...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
